      "source": [
        "# Neural-network formal verification demos\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook contains four presentation-oriented experiments developed\n",
        "in this project. Each property is checked with both **α,β-CROWN** and\n",
        "**Marabou**.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Demo | Model | Verified boundary | Formal claim |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| A | NASA MicroNet-pretrained ResNet-18 | Exact final linear layer, 512 learned microscopy features | Nominal output remains above its nominal runner-up |\n",
        "| B | NASA Airfoil Learning MLP | Exact reduced network with geometry fixed and three operating inputs variable | Selected aerodynamic coefficient remains within a stated tolerance |\n",
        "| C | Official NASA-IMPACT Division Classifier | Exact final linear layer, 768 learned document features | Predicted NASA division remains above all four alternatives |\n",
        "| D | NASA GIBS anomaly architecture | Complete 256-feature, 100-hidden-unit ReLU classifier | Normal/miscoloration decision is preserved |\n",
        "\n",
        "Demos A and C use official downloadable NASA checkpoints. Demo B follows an\n",
        "official NASA architecture and trains on NASA's processed Airfoil Learning\n",
        "data. Demo D reproduces the official NASA GIBS neural architecture on real\n",
        "GIBS satellite images with controlled miscoloration examples. NASA does not\n",
        "publish pretrained checkpoints for B or D, so the notebook trains those\n",
        "models reproducibly and labels them accordingly.\n",
        "\n",
        "## How to interpret the tools\n",
        "\n",
        "- **α,β-CROWN** proves that the required output margins remain positive over\n",
        "  the entire bounded input region.\n",
        "- **Marabou** searches for a violation. `unsat` means that no violating input\n",
        "  exists, so the property is proved.\n",
        "- These are universal statements over continuous boxes, not random tests.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
