      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d91bcfc3",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d91bcfc3"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Demo B — NASA Airfoil Learning model\n",
        "\n",
        "NASA's [`airfoil-learning`](https://github.com/nasa/airfoil-learning)\n",
        "project trains multilayer perceptrons to predict aerodynamic coefficients\n",
        "from airfoil geometry and operating conditions. This notebook reproduces an\n",
        "official configuration:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "airfoil geometry + angle of attack + Reynolds number + Ncrit\n",
        "  → 64 → ReLU6 → 64 → ReLU6 → 64 → ReLU6 → 64 → ReLU6\n",
        "  → Cl, Cd, Cdp, Cm\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "For verification, the airfoil geometry is fixed exactly. Its contribution\n",
        "is absorbed into the first-layer bias, leaving an exactly equivalent network\n",
        "with three variable inputs. We prove\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "  \\lVert u-u_0\\rVert_\\infty\\le 0.001\n",
        "  \\Longrightarrow\n",
        "  |\\widehat C_l(u)-\\widehat C_l(u_0)|<0.01,\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "where all three operating inputs are NASA's min-max-normalized values. This\n",
        "is a network-output stability claim, not a bound on physical-model error.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d7d1294e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d7d1294e"
      },
      "source": [
        "## B1. Download only the required NASA training tensor\n",
        "\n",
        "NASA's complete processed archive is about 8.6 GB. `RemoteZip` uses HTTP\n",
        "range requests to retrieve only the required min-max-normalized DNN tensor\n",
        "(roughly 0.5 GB transferred), making this substantially more practical in\n",
        "Colab.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "466ce6eb",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "466ce6eb",
        "outputId": "a7ec5e33-7c97-4a6c-afbc-ca13be0811a6"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Retrieving the single required member from NASA's archive...\n",
            "Uncompressed member size (MB): 911.3\n",
            "NASA Airfoil tensor: /content/airfoil-data/dnn_scaled_data_train.pt\n",
            "Downloaded size (MB): 911.3\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "!test -d /content/airfoil-learning || git clone -q https://github.com/nasa/airfoil-learning.git /content/airfoil-learning\n",
        "\n",
        "from remotezip import RemoteZip\n",
        "import shutil\n",
        "\n",
        "AIRFOIL_ARCHIVE = \"https://nasa-public-data.s3.amazonaws.com/plot3d_utilities/dataset-processed.zip\"\n",
        "AIRFOIL_MEMBER = \"datasets/minmax/dnn_scaled_data_train.pt\"\n",
        "airfoil_data_path = Path(\"/content/airfoil-data/dnn_scaled_data_train.pt\")\n",
        "airfoil_data_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "if not airfoil_data_path.exists():\n",
        "    print(\"Retrieving the single required member from NASA's archive...\")\n",
        "    with RemoteZip(AIRFOIL_ARCHIVE) as archive:\n",
        "        info = archive.getinfo(AIRFOIL_MEMBER)\n",
        "        print(\"Uncompressed member size (MB):\", round(info.file_size / 1e6, 1))\n",
        "        with archive.open(AIRFOIL_MEMBER) as source, open(airfoil_data_path, \"wb\") as target:\n",
        "            shutil.copyfileobj(source, target, length=8 * 1024 * 1024)\n",
        "print(\"NASA Airfoil tensor:\", airfoil_data_path)\n",
        "print(\"Downloaded size (MB):\", round(airfoil_data_path.stat().st_size / 1e6, 1))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "67024610",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "67024610"
      },
      "source": [
        "## B2. Train the NASA architecture reproducibly\n",
        "\n",
        "The repository publishes training code and data but not a pretrained\n",
        "checkpoint. Therefore this is an official NASA architecture retrained in\n",
        "the notebook—not a NASA-released checkpoint.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4ceafebe",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "4ceafebe",
        "outputId": "c57c763b-4553-4f60-94c7-53e33faeb444"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Writing /content/train_airfoil_combined.py\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "%%writefile /content/train_airfoil_combined.py\n",
        "import json, random, torch, torch.nn as nn\n",
        "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, TensorDataset\n",
        "\n",
        "SEED=42; random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
        "device=torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
        "raw=torch.load(\"/content/airfoil-data/dnn_scaled_data_train.pt\",map_location=\"cpu\",weights_only=False)\n",
        "count=min(50_000,len(raw)); selected=torch.randperm(len(raw),generator=torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED))[:count]\n",
        "X=torch.stack([raw[int(i)][0].float().flatten() for i in selected])\n",
        "Y=torch.stack([raw[int(i)][1].float().flatten()[:4] for i in selected])\n",
        "split=int(.85*count); train=DataLoader(TensorDataset(X[:split],Y[:split]),batch_size=512,shuffle=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "class AirfoilMLP(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self,d):\n",
        "        super().__init__(); dims=[d,64,64,64,64,4]\n",
        "        self.layers=nn.ModuleList([nn.Linear(dims[i],dims[i+1]) for i in range(len(dims)-1)])\n",
        "    def forward(self,x):\n",
        "        for layer in self.layers[:-1]:\n",
        "            z=layer(x); x=torch.relu(z)-torch.relu(z-6.0)\n",
        "        return self.layers[-1](x)\n",
        "\n",
        "model=AirfoilMLP(X.shape[1]).to(device); opt=torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(),lr=1e-3,weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
        "for epoch in range(1,26):\n",
        "    model.train(); total=0.0\n",
        "    for xb,yb in train:\n",
        "        xb=xb.to(device); yb=yb.to(device); opt.zero_grad()\n",
        "        loss=nn.functional.mse_loss(model(xb),yb); loss.backward(); opt.step(); total+=loss.item()*len(xb)\n",
        "    if epoch==1 or epoch%5==0:\n",
        "        model.eval()\n",
        "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "            val=model(X[split:].to(device)).cpu(); mae=(val-Y[split:]).abs().mean(0)\n",
        "        print(f\"epoch {epoch:02d} | train MSE {total/split:.6g} | validation MAE {mae.tolist()}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "model.eval()\n",
        "with torch.no_grad(): val=model(X[split:].to(device)).cpu()\n",
        "errors=(val-Y[split:]).abs().mean(1); idx=int(torch.argmin(errors))\n",
        "checkpoint={\"state_dict\":model.cpu().state_dict(),\"input_dimension\":X.shape[1],\n",
        "    \"sample_x\":X[split+idx],\"sample_target\":Y[split+idx],\"sample_prediction\":val[idx]}\n",
        "torch.save(checkpoint,\"/content/airfoil_demo.pt\")\n",
        "print(\"Saved /content/airfoil_demo.pt\")\n",
        "print(\"Input dimension:\",X.shape[1])\n",
        "print(\"Selected predictions [Cl, Cd, Cdp, Cm]:\",val[idx].tolist())\n",
        "print(\"Selected targets     [Cl, Cd, Cdp, Cm]:\",Y[split+idx].tolist())\n"
      ]
    },
