      "source": [
        "# Demo D — NASA GIBS satellite-image anomaly classifier\n",
        "\n",
        "NASA's official [`gibs-ml`](https://github.com/nasa-gibs/gibs-ml)\n",
        "project detects validation anomalies such as miscoloration in Earth\n",
        "satellite imagery. Its published neural classifier is:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "256-bin HSV hue histogram → Linear(100) → ReLU → Linear(2)\n",
        "                          → normal / abnormal logits\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The repository provides this architecture and training notebook but no\n",
        "pretrained checkpoint. We reproduce the architecture on real daily NASA\n",
        "VIIRS/GIBS images and controlled hue-shift miscolorations. This creates a\n",
        "deterministic, downloadable benchmark while being explicit that the weights\n",
        "are retrained for this demonstration.\n",
        "\n",
        "Both tools verify the complete nonlinear neural classifier from its 256\n",
        "input features to the binary decision. The result is feature-level rather\n",
        "than raw-pixel robustness because histogram extraction is outside the neural\n",
        "network.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e0b80ee3",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e0b80ee3"
      },
      "source": [
        "## D1. Download real NASA GIBS images and construct controlled anomalies\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "365b9b46",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 256
        },
        "id": "365b9b46",
        "outputId": "2813b38f-5915-46d4-ca1e-fb33790f4e5f"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Skipped 2024-07-15 — HTTP Error 404: Not Found\n",
            "Downloaded daily GIBS images: 35\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1200x400 with 2 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import datetime, io, urllib.request\n",
        "from matplotlib import colors as mcolors\n",
        "\n",
        "def gibs_url(date):\n",
        "    return (\n",
        "        \"https://gibs-c.earthdata.nasa.gov/wmts/epsg4326/best/wmts.cgi?\"\n",
        "        f\"TIME={date}T00:00:00Z&layer=VIIRS_SNPP_CorrectedReflectance_TrueColor\"\n",
        "        \"&style=default&tilematrixset=250m&Service=WMTS&Request=GetTile\"\n",
        "        \"&Version=1.0.0&Format=image%2Fjpeg&TileMatrix=0&TileCol=0&TileRow=0\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "def northern_crop(image):\n",
        "    return image.crop((0, 0, image.width, image.height // 2)).resize((256, 128))\n",
        "\n",
        "def controlled_miscoloration(image, hue_shift=0.28):\n",
        "    arr=np.asarray(northern_crop(image),dtype=np.float32)/255.0\n",
        "    hsv=mcolors.rgb_to_hsv(arr); hsv[...,0]=(hsv[...,0]+hue_shift)%1.0\n",
        "    rgb=np.uint8(np.clip(mcolors.hsv_to_rgb(hsv),0,1)*255)\n",
        "    return Image.fromarray(rgb)\n",
        "\n",
        "gibs_dates=[f\"{year}-{month:02d}-15\" for year in (2022,2023,2024) for month in range(1,13)]\n",
        "gibs_images=[]\n",
        "for date in gibs_dates:\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        with urllib.request.urlopen(gibs_url(date),timeout=30) as response:\n",
        "            gibs_images.append((date,Image.open(io.BytesIO(response.read())).convert(\"RGB\")))\n",
        "    except Exception as error:\n",
        "        print(\"Skipped\",date,\"—\",error)\n",
        "assert len(gibs_images)>=24, \"Too few GIBS dates were available\"\n",
        "print(\"Downloaded daily GIBS images:\",len(gibs_images))\n",
        "\n",
        "gibs_clean=northern_crop(gibs_images[0][1]); gibs_bad=controlled_miscoloration(gibs_images[0][1])\n",
        "gibs_clean.save(\"/content/gibs_nominal.png\"); gibs_bad.save(\"/content/gibs_controlled_anomaly.png\")\n",
        "fig,axes=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(12,4))\n",
        "axes[0].imshow(gibs_clean); axes[0].set_title(\"Real NASA GIBS image — normal\"); axes[0].axis(\"off\")\n",
        "axes[1].imshow(gibs_bad); axes[1].set_title(\"Controlled hue miscoloration — abnormal\"); axes[1].axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "66a6e7be",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "66a6e7be"
      },
      "source": [
        "## D2. Reproduce NASA's two-layer classifier and choose a certifiable example\n",
        "\n",
        "The uncertainty radius is selected analytically so every hidden ReLU keeps\n",
        "its activation state and the normal-minus-abnormal margin remains positive.\n",
        "This makes the subsequent formal proofs conclusive rather than relying on a\n",
        "guessed epsilon.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "fb095abe",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "fb095abe",
        "outputId": "bd4019d1-dac8-4c88-a936-523263f47522"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Training / validation / test accuracy: 1.0 1.0 1.0\n",
            "Selected clean test date: 2022-12-15\n",
            "Nominal normal-minus-abnormal margin: 5.384053707122803\n",
            "ReLU-stability radius: 0.005187690258026123\n",
            "Affine decision radius: 0.00899101234972477\n",
            "Verification epsilon: 0.0025938451290130615\n",
            "Exact lower margin within stable region: 3.8307913580792956\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stderr",
          "text": [
            "/tmp/ipykernel_796/3744772453.py:78: DeprecationWarning: You are using the legacy TorchScript-based ONNX export. Starting in PyTorch 2.9, the new torch.export-based ONNX exporter has become the default. Learn more about the new export logic: https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/onnx_export.html. For exporting control flow: https://pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/onnx/export_control_flow_model_to_onnx_tutorial.html\n",
            "  torch.onnx.export(gibs_margin,gibs_x0,\"/content/gibs_margin.onnx\",input_names=[\"gibs_hue_features\"],\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def gibs_hue_histogram(image):\n",
        "    arr=np.asarray(northern_crop(image),dtype=np.float32)/255.0\n",
        "    hue=mcolors.rgb_to_hsv(arr)[...,0]\n",
        "    hist,_=np.histogram(hue,bins=np.linspace(0,1,257),density=False)\n",
        "    return hist.astype(np.float32)/hue.size\n",
        "\n",
        "rng=np.random.default_rng(7); order=rng.permutation(len(gibs_images))\n",
        "n_train=int(.70*len(order)); n_val=max(4,int(.15*len(order)))\n",
        "train_ids=order[:n_train]; val_ids=order[n_train:n_train+n_val]; test_ids=order[n_train+n_val:]\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_examples(indices):\n",
        "    feats=[]; labels=[]; dates=[]\n",
        "    for idx in indices:\n",
        "        date,image=gibs_images[int(idx)]\n",
        "        feats.extend([gibs_hue_histogram(image),gibs_hue_histogram(controlled_miscoloration(image))])\n",
        "        labels.extend([0,1]); dates.extend([date,date])\n",
        "    return np.stack(feats),np.array(labels,dtype=np.int64),dates\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train,y_train,_=make_examples(train_ids); X_val,y_val,_=make_examples(val_ids); X_test,y_test,test_dates=make_examples(test_ids)\n",
        "feature_mean=X_train.mean(0,keepdims=True)\n",
        "X_train-=feature_mean; X_val-=feature_mean; X_test-=feature_mean\n",
        "tx=torch.tensor(X_train); ty=torch.tensor(y_train); vx=torch.tensor(X_val); vy=torch.tensor(y_val); qx=torch.tensor(X_test); qy=torch.tensor(y_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "class GIBSTwoLayerNet(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self):\n",
        "        super().__init__(); self.fc1=nn.Linear(256,100); self.fc2=nn.Linear(100,2)\n",
        "    def forward(self,x): return self.fc2(torch.relu(self.fc1(x)))\n",
        "\n",
        "torch.manual_seed(7); gibs_model=GIBSTwoLayerNet(); optimizer=torch.optim.Adam(gibs_model.parameters(),lr=1e-2,weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
        "for step in range(500):\n",
        "    optimizer.zero_grad(); loss=nn.functional.cross_entropy(gibs_model(tx),ty); loss.backward(); optimizer.step()\n",
        "gibs_model.eval()\n",
        "with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "    train_acc=float((gibs_model(tx).argmax(1)==ty).float().mean())\n",
        "    val_acc=float((gibs_model(vx).argmax(1)==vy).float().mean())\n",
        "    test_pred=gibs_model(qx).argmax(1); test_acc=float((test_pred==qy).float().mean())\n",
        "\n",
        "candidates=torch.where((qy==0)&(test_pred==0))[0]\n",
        "robustness=[]\n",
        "with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "    for idx in candidates:\n",
        "        sample=qx[idx]; pre=gibs_model.fc1(sample); first_l1=gibs_model.fc1.weight.abs().sum(1)\n",
        "        stable=torch.where(first_l1>0,pre.abs()/first_l1,torch.tensor(float(\"inf\"))).min()\n",
        "        margin_weights=gibs_model.fc2.weight[0]-gibs_model.fc2.weight[1]\n",
        "        effective=(margin_weights*(pre>0).float())@gibs_model.fc1.weight\n",
        "        margin=gibs_model(sample)[0]-gibs_model(sample)[1]\n",
        "        decision=margin/effective.abs().sum(); radius=torch.minimum(stable,decision)\n",
        "        robustness.append((float(radius),int(idx),float(stable),float(decision),float(margin)))\n",
        "assert robustness,\"No correctly classified normal test image was available\"\n",
        "gibs_radius,gibs_index,gibs_stability_radius,gibs_decision_radius,gibs_nominal_margin=max(robustness)\n",
        "gibs_epsilon=gibs_radius/2; gibs_x0=qx[gibs_index:gibs_index+1]\n",
        "\n",
        "gibs_margin=nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(256,100),nn.ReLU(),nn.Linear(100,1))\n",
        "with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "    gibs_margin[0].weight.copy_(gibs_model.fc1.weight); gibs_margin[0].bias.copy_(gibs_model.fc1.bias)\n",
        "    gibs_margin[2].weight.copy_(gibs_model.fc2.weight[0:1]-gibs_model.fc2.weight[1:2])\n",
        "    gibs_margin[2].bias.copy_(gibs_model.fc2.bias[0:1]-gibs_model.fc2.bias[1:2])\n",
        "    gibs_exact_lower=gibs_nominal_margin-gibs_epsilon*(((gibs_margin[2].weight[0]*(gibs_model.fc1(gibs_x0)[0]>0).float())@gibs_model.fc1.weight).abs().sum().item())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Training / validation / test accuracy:\",train_acc,val_acc,test_acc)\n",
        "print(\"Selected clean test date:\",test_dates[gibs_index])\n",
        "print(\"Nominal normal-minus-abnormal margin:\",gibs_nominal_margin)\n",
        "print(\"ReLU-stability radius:\",gibs_stability_radius)\n",
        "print(\"Affine decision radius:\",gibs_decision_radius)\n",
        "print(\"Verification epsilon:\",gibs_epsilon)\n",
        "print(\"Exact lower margin within stable region:\",gibs_exact_lower)\n",
        "assert gibs_exact_lower>0\n",
        "\n",
        "np.save(\"/content/gibs_x0.npy\",gibs_x0.numpy().astype(np.float32))\n",
        "np.savez(\"/content/gibs_parameters.npz\",w0=gibs_margin[0].weight.detach().numpy().astype(np.float32),\n",
        "    b0=gibs_margin[0].bias.detach().numpy().astype(np.float32),w1=gibs_margin[2].weight.detach().numpy().astype(np.float32),\n",
        "    b1=gibs_margin[2].bias.detach().numpy().astype(np.float32))\n",
        "gibs_meta={\"model\":\"NASA GIBS TwoLayerNet architecture retrained for this demo\",\"feature_dimension\":256,\n",
        "    \"hidden_units\":100,\"selected_date\":test_dates[gibs_index],\"verification_epsilon\":gibs_epsilon,\n",
        "    \"nominal_margin\":gibs_nominal_margin,\"exact_lower_margin\":gibs_exact_lower,\"train_accuracy\":train_acc,\n",
        "    \"validation_accuracy\":val_acc,\"test_accuracy\":test_acc,\"scope\":\"complete neural classifier from hue-histogram features to binary decision\"}\n",
        "json.dump(gibs_meta,open(\"/content/gibs_meta.json\",\"w\"),indent=2)\n",
        "torch.onnx.export(gibs_margin,gibs_x0,\"/content/gibs_margin.onnx\",input_names=[\"gibs_hue_features\"],\n",
        "    output_names=[\"normal_minus_abnormal_margin\"],opset_version=17,do_constant_folding=True,dynamo=False)\n",
        "onnx.checker.check_model(onnx.load(\"/content/gibs_margin.onnx\"))\n"
      ]
    },
